Read ALL four v6 verdicts, the FULL v7 design and its diff from v6, the oracle README and evidence files, the oracle source/test, and check claims against actual Java and current Go. v7 answers v6: every task-kind capability error is raised at Java's CONSUMER point after the task's no-op exits (no pre-removal/pre-claim check; the transaction abort rolls back the removal), with MEASURED obsolete-task consumption under collapse/reassign/merge knobs and the KMeans false-alarm golden; the livelock rows are one mechanism (empty neighbour list = not fetched) refused where Java writes the empty-list task, with the immutable neighbour-count knobs declared permanent; config-only insert refusal withdrawn except insertMaxCandidateClusters<1 (measured never searchable), enqueue refusal added to the poison list; RaBitQ refusal at Primitives.quantizer construction points; inline deletes MEASURED (they fail wherever inline inserts fail) with the declared skip (d); record-layer inline via autoMergeDuringCommit MEASURED; split throw site: ITERATED outlier peel bounded at 8 refits, MEASURED usable within 5 refits at 8 seeds on two-opposite-outliers, nested, scattered, 60/40@0.45 and heavy-tail shapes on which the target throws forever in both modes; step-2 population restated; an inline-mode cap keyed to the reconcile's residue state (count+1 > hardMax and neither SPLIT_MERGE nor COLLAPSE) with its Java-healthy firing window enumerated; operation-order wording fixed (tag-5 move, UUID not from op RNG); foreign-lease wait slices min(own lease,10s)/3 through refreshFollowupHeartbeats; claim-race loser enters the wait; relieved read is a post-commit snapshot; merge lease carve-out from byte-for-byte; replay wording reconciled with the engine-identity guard. Challenge sufficiency and interactions with the rest of the design, not only whether the requested words appear. Distinguish measured target facts from remaining source hypotheses.
